From: cv610-fpv
Subject: [PATCH] hi3516cv6xx imx335: 2-lane crop and flex modes up to 1080p100 / 864p120

On top of 0001 (2-lane mode 0). The 1080p crop table, which the flex
window-crop mode (Isp_SnsMode=5) replays, was a 4-lane table at 594 Mbit/s;
it now carries the stock-firmware 2-lane INCK/analog block with SYS_MODE
0x01 (1188 Mbit/s per lane) and LANEMODE 2.

Two limits set the shortest usable line, both measured on a Hi3516CV610-20S
+ IMX335 2-lane board:
 - lane bandwidth: a RAW10 row of HNUM pixels within 2H on two lanes; at
   1080p HMAX 308 truncates frames, 317 is clean (5% margin kept);
 - the sensor minimum line 0x113: 1536x864 at HMAX 269 comes out streaked.
Rates above that floor are refused in cmos_isp_set_image_mode() and
cmos_fps_set() instead of streaming broken frames.

Flex VMAX now follows the window (it was held at the 1080p table's
0x08F8), so windows under 1080 lines can reach 120 fps on two lanes.

Verified: 1080p60/90/100 and 1536x864@120, no MIPI CRC/ECC errors, clean
image, full rate at VPSS and in the H.265 RTP output (waybeam and majestic).
1080p110 is refused (limit ~101 fps).

